---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Terms of Service — Zachary Routsong Photography">
<style is:global>
.terms-page {
  max-width: 680px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 56px 28px 96px;
}
.terms-page h1 {
  font-size: 26px;
  font-weight: 300;
  letter-spacing: -.02em;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.terms-meta {
  font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: .1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--text-3);
  margin-bottom: 36px;
}
.terms-page h2 {
  font-size: 15px;
  font-weight: 500;
  margin-top: 36px;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
  color: var(--text);
}
.terms-page p {
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--text-2);
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.terms-page ul {
  margin: 0 0 12px 0;
  padding-left: 18px;
}
.terms-page ul li {
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--text-2);
  margin-bottom: 3px;
}
.terms-page a { color: var(--text); text-decoration: underline; }
.terms-page a:hover { opacity: .7; }
.terms-divider {
  border: none;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  margin: 28px 0;
}
</style>

<div class="terms-page">
  <div class="sec-label" style="margin-bottom:8px">legal</div>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="terms-meta">Effective July 2026</p>

  <p>These are the plain-English terms for booking a photo session with Zachary Routsong Photography. Booking a session means you agree to them. If anything here is unclear, just ask before you book.</p>

  <hr class="terms-divider"/>

  <h2>Booking and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Submitting a request on this site does not lock in a session — it's a request. You'll get an email once it's accepted, with a link to finalize the details.</li>
    <li>A <strong>50% deposit</strong> secures your date once your booking is confirmed. The remaining balance is due on the day of the session.</li>
    <li>The price you see at booking (including any promo code you applied) is the price — plus any add-ons or travel fee you choose at confirmation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rescheduling and cancellations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Need to move or cancel? Give at least <strong>48 hours' notice</strong> and your deposit transfers to the new date, or gets refunded if you cancel outright.</li>
    <li>Cancellations with less than 48 hours' notice (or no-shows) may forfeit the deposit — that time was reserved for you.</li>
    <li>Weather or genuine emergencies: we'll reschedule at no cost. Life happens.</li>
    <li>If Zachary has to cancel for any reason, you get a full refund of anything paid, or priority rebooking — your choice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Photo delivery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edited photos are delivered through a private online gallery, typically within 5–7 days of your session.</li>
    <li>Galleries stay online for roughly 90 days — download your photos during that window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Copyright and how photos can be used</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Zachary retains the copyright to all images, as is standard for photographers.</li>
    <li>You receive a <strong>personal-use license</strong>: print your photos, share them, post them — freely and forever. Selling them or using them commercially requires separate written permission.</li>
    <li>Your photos appear in Zachary's portfolio or social media <strong>only if you said it's OK</strong> (there's an optional checkbox at booking). You can change your mind either way, anytime — just reach out.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If something goes wrong</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>In the unlikely event of equipment failure, illness, or lost images, liability is limited to a reshoot or a refund of what you've paid — whichever you prefer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Call or text <a href="tel:2293001006">229-300-1006</a>, or reach out on Instagram <a href="https://instagram.com/zacharyroutsongphotos" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@zacharyroutsongphotos</a>.</p>

  <hr class="terms-divider"/>

  <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-3);line-height:1.8">If these terms change meaningfully, the date at the top gets updated. See also the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</div>
</Layout>
